1
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,083
[Seoul Namgang Police Station]

2
00:00:43,083 --> 00:00:45,000
Am I hearing this right?

3
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,959
The burned corpse could be Hyun Kyung?

4
00:00:48,959 --> 00:00:51,542
What kind of investigation were you doing?

5
00:00:51,542 --> 00:00:53,334
Wait, wait, wait.

6
00:00:53,334 --> 00:00:56,500
Just wait. When will the result be out?

7
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:59,709
The autopsy will begin shortly.
NFS will tell us as soon as they know.

8
00:00:59,709 --> 00:01:02,876
Shouldn't we go there and hurry things up?

9
00:01:02,876 --> 00:01:04,459
They're doing the autopsy.

10
00:01:04,459 --> 00:01:07,584
You can't hurry this kind of work.

11
00:01:07,584 --> 00:01:09,209
I guess not.

12
00:01:09,834 --> 00:01:13,334
Won't they need something to test against?

13
00:01:13,334 --> 00:01:17,584
I collected some hair from her comb.

14
00:01:18,250 --> 00:01:20,083
They can run a DNA test with it.

15
00:01:20,083 --> 00:01:22,876
It can't be her, can it? No way, it can't.

16
00:01:22,876 --> 00:01:25,334
There is no way, right?

17
00:01:25,334 --> 00:01:27,709
Fidgeting won't help.

18
00:01:27,709 --> 00:01:29,417
Let's stay calm and wait.

19
00:01:29,417 --> 00:01:31,709
It's not something to be calm about.

20
00:01:31,709 --> 00:01:35,209
If it is her, we're done for. All of us!

21
00:01:35,209 --> 00:01:38,334
Okay, maybe it's not about us.

22
00:01:38,334 --> 00:01:40,751
But what do we say to her family?

23
00:01:40,751 --> 00:01:43,042
Who will notify her next of kin?

24
00:01:43,042 --> 00:01:44,542
Who is it?

25
00:01:48,417 --> 00:01:51,250
I heard about Detective Eo.

26
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:53,334
What's the status?

27
00:01:54,125 --> 00:01:57,250
Well, the thing is,

28
00:01:57,250 --> 00:01:58,834
the status…

29
00:02:00,042 --> 00:02:02,083
It is very serious and-

30
00:02:02,083 --> 00:02:04,500
We sent the body to NFS,

31
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:08,083
and the DNA result is expected
within today at the earliest.

32
00:02:10,667 --> 00:02:14,083
This is her dental record.

33
00:02:15,083 --> 00:02:18,834
X-ray and medical records included.
If it's really Hyun-

34
00:02:21,709 --> 00:02:24,250
If it's Detective Eo, these will tell you.

35
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:26,000
But, Ma'am,

36
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,542
why do you have her records?

37
00:02:28,542 --> 00:02:29,626
I mean-

38
00:02:29,626 --> 00:02:31,334
She's her daughter.

39
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:37,083
Detective Eo is her daughter.

40
00:02:37,083 --> 00:02:38,959
Her only daughter.

41
00:02:41,417 --> 00:02:44,626
Wait, what are you…

42
00:02:44,626 --> 00:02:47,292
Her daughter is Eo Hyun Kyung?

43
00:02:47,292 --> 00:02:49,667
Hold on,

44
00:02:49,667 --> 00:02:51,375
And Hyun Kyung's mother is…

45
00:02:51,375 --> 00:02:53,876
Chief Shin?

46
00:02:53,876 --> 00:02:56,959
Oh my god, oh my god.

47
00:02:58,042 --> 00:02:59,542
Oh my god.

48
00:03:01,667 --> 00:03:03,167
Chief Shin. Just look at her.

49
00:03:03,167 --> 00:03:06,626
As a fellow woman, I can't help but admire her.

50
00:03:06,626 --> 00:03:08,876
But she looks oddly familiar.

51
00:03:08,876 --> 00:03:12,542
She does. Did I see her somewhere before?

52
00:03:12,542 --> 00:03:16,918
Maybe she just has a common face.

53
00:03:16,918 --> 00:03:20,375
Let's go. Lunch, anyone?

54
00:03:20,375 --> 00:03:22,459
Where did you get the news?

55
00:03:22,459 --> 00:03:25,876
Just hear and there.

56
00:03:38,918 --> 00:03:42,250
[Episode 4]

57
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:46,125
Now I understand why she's been
so quiet about her family.

58
00:03:49,167 --> 00:03:51,459
How could she hide it even from me?

59
00:03:51,459 --> 00:03:53,250
Who told the Chief about the corpse, anyway?

60
00:03:53,250 --> 00:03:57,417
Someone who knows that
Detective Eo is her daughter.

61
00:03:57,417 --> 00:04:01,417
Someone who knew it all along.

62
00:04:02,167 --> 00:04:03,751
Oh, Captain.

63
00:04:09,417 --> 00:04:10,834
Where are you going?

64
00:04:10,834 --> 00:04:12,083
To do whatever I can.

65
00:04:12,083 --> 00:04:15,626
I'm going to search where Detective Eo
made her last call.

66
00:04:15,626 --> 00:04:16,834
Yeah.

67
00:04:16,834 --> 00:04:19,542
Let's do that. We gotta do something.

68
00:04:19,542 --> 00:04:20,542
Dong Gi, let's go!

69
00:04:20,542 --> 00:04:22,459
Okay, I'll go too.

70
00:04:38,417 --> 00:04:40,918
[National Office Of Investigation]

71
00:04:46,042 --> 00:04:48,042
You know the Pastor, right?

72
00:04:48,042 --> 00:04:49,918
Where's the Pastor?

73
00:04:54,876 --> 00:04:58,500
What about the name? The real name.

74
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,000
No idea.

75
00:05:01,667 --> 00:05:03,542
No idea?

76
00:05:04,167 --> 00:05:06,626
Not even the name?

77
00:05:06,626 --> 00:05:09,000
We don't share names.

78
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,834
Haven't seen each other. We don't even call.

79
00:05:11,834 --> 00:05:13,584
We only use Telegram.

80
00:05:18,584 --> 00:05:20,083
Na Hae Ju.

81
00:05:20,083 --> 00:05:22,375
She's the Pastor, right?

82
00:05:22,959 --> 00:05:25,500
Did she say that? That she's the Pastor?

83
00:05:26,125 --> 00:05:27,584
Seriously.

84
00:05:27,584 --> 00:05:30,792
Stop pretending you don't know.
You knew all along.

85
00:05:31,459 --> 00:05:32,834
I said I don't.

86
00:05:32,834 --> 00:05:35,876
If she says she's the Pastor, then maybe she is.

87
00:05:36,626 --> 00:05:38,209
I don't have a clue.

88
00:05:38,876 --> 00:05:40,918
Why you little…

89
00:05:47,042 --> 00:05:50,709
Would you… like anything to drink?

90
00:05:50,709 --> 00:05:52,292
No thank you.

91
00:05:52,292 --> 00:05:53,834
I'm good.

92
00:05:55,125 --> 00:05:56,709
Director Son.

93
00:05:56,709 --> 00:05:58,751
You like Yulmucha, right?

94
00:06:01,459 --> 00:06:03,584
Maybe not.

95
00:06:03,584 --> 00:06:05,918
I stopped drinking it years ago.

96
00:06:05,918 --> 00:06:08,292
I'm not thirsty, either. You go ahead.

97
00:06:12,542 --> 00:06:14,375
Excuse me.

98
00:06:14,375 --> 00:06:18,000
I have highly irritable bowels.

99
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,209
And I was under a lot of stress today, so…

100
00:06:20,209 --> 00:06:24,167
Oh my, oh my. Excuse me.

101
00:06:24,167 --> 00:06:25,792
Please excuse me.

102
00:06:39,542 --> 00:06:42,334
Her teammates didn't know, then.

103
00:06:42,334 --> 00:06:45,250
Detective Eo was so adamant.

104
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:47,876
She felt she couldn't prove herself

105
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:50,834
if she's known as someone's daughter.

106
00:06:52,417 --> 00:06:54,792
Like mother, like daughter.

107
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:00,876
She's been like that for a long time.

108
00:07:02,167 --> 00:07:04,250
She didn't like me coming to her school.

109
00:07:04,792 --> 00:07:09,167
Didn't even let me attend
the parents' events at school.

110
00:07:09,167 --> 00:07:12,959
She applied to the force
without telling me first.

111
00:07:16,751 --> 00:07:18,959
I found out after she got accepted.

112
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:28,417
I'm sorry. I failed as her commander.

113
00:07:34,459 --> 00:07:36,667
- What's the status?
- Nothing we can do.

114
00:07:41,959 --> 00:07:43,584
No pulse here, either.

115
00:07:50,292 --> 00:07:52,542
- Let no one in.
- Yes, Ma'am.

116
00:08:01,459 --> 00:08:03,709
Oh, darling.

117
00:08:03,709 --> 00:08:06,751
Oh, poor darling.

118
00:08:06,751 --> 00:08:10,250
It's okay, it's okay.

119
00:08:10,250 --> 00:08:11,584
So Jung?

120
00:08:11,584 --> 00:08:15,042
She survived. Isn't she brave?

121
00:08:15,042 --> 00:08:17,751
Oh my god.

122
00:08:17,751 --> 00:08:20,792
Okay, baby.

123
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:27,876
This won't do. Let me.

124
00:08:27,876 --> 00:08:31,542
- Everything's okay.
- There, there.

125
00:08:33,042 --> 00:08:35,500
She doesn't cry when you hold her.

126
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:37,042
I know, right?

127
00:08:37,042 --> 00:08:40,334
Where do you wanna go? Where?

128
00:08:44,167 --> 00:08:46,083
She's a strong girl.

129
00:08:47,292 --> 00:08:48,876
She must be all right.

130
00:08:50,918 --> 00:08:52,584
I'm sure of it.

131
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:08,209
Her last call came through this cell tower.

132
00:09:10,918 --> 00:09:14,042
Dong Gi, get CCTV footage.
Both of us split up and search.

133
00:09:14,042 --> 00:09:15,292
- Okay.
- Okay.

134
00:09:39,584 --> 00:09:42,918
[Anjail Car Rental]

135
00:09:44,876 --> 00:09:46,709
A car rental.

136
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,125
[Anjail Car Rental]

137
00:10:09,292 --> 00:10:10,751
[53 HU 5844]

138
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:18,083
Illegitimate plates.

139
00:10:18,667 --> 00:10:20,500
[33 HEU 5249]

140
00:10:21,125 --> 00:10:22,626
5249.

141
00:10:27,709 --> 00:10:30,083
Lieutenant, it's me!

142
00:10:30,083 --> 00:10:31,626
Are you all right, Inspector Cha?

143
00:10:31,626 --> 00:10:33,375
- I'm okay.
- Oh, come on!

144
00:10:33,375 --> 00:10:34,709
Why?

145
00:10:34,709 --> 00:10:37,459
Why sneak up on me like that?

146
00:10:37,459 --> 00:10:39,000
Sorry.

147
00:10:40,792 --> 00:10:42,792
Look here. 5249.

148
00:10:42,792 --> 00:10:44,375
This is the one she was moved in.

149
00:10:44,375 --> 00:10:47,250
Detective Eo must have been here.

150
00:10:47,250 --> 00:10:48,667
This way.

151
00:10:54,876 --> 00:10:56,292
What's this?

152
00:10:58,584 --> 00:10:59,751
Blood?

153
00:10:59,751 --> 00:11:02,250
Judging by the state, it's been a day or so.

154
00:11:02,250 --> 00:11:04,167
It means… this blood…

155
00:11:05,334 --> 00:11:07,083
Might be from Detective Eo.

156
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,918
Namgang Station, TCI.

157
00:11:24,584 --> 00:11:25,918
What?

158
00:11:28,334 --> 00:11:29,751
Knock first!

159
00:11:29,751 --> 00:11:32,417
It's not! It's not Detective Eo!

160
00:11:32,417 --> 00:11:34,125
- You got the call?
- Yes, from NOI.

161
00:11:34,125 --> 00:11:36,209
I mean, NFS.

162
00:11:36,209 --> 00:11:37,250
So Jung.

163
00:11:37,250 --> 00:11:41,375
Okay! That's it!

164
00:11:41,959 --> 00:11:43,667
Oh my.

165
00:11:43,667 --> 00:11:46,125
Congratulations, Ma'am.

166
00:11:46,125 --> 00:11:47,709
That's inappropriate!

167
00:11:47,709 --> 00:11:49,083
A person's dead!

168
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:50,417
That's right, but-

169
00:11:50,417 --> 00:11:52,459
Then who is it?

170
00:11:52,459 --> 00:11:55,000
- It's…
- Na Hae Ju?

171
00:11:56,167 --> 00:11:58,792
Yeah. Okay, got it.

172
00:11:58,792 --> 00:12:01,083
Which one's Na Hae Ju? The corpse from the car?

173
00:12:01,083 --> 00:12:04,375
Yes, NFS called. What's going on here?

174
00:12:04,375 --> 00:12:07,125
So Na Hae Ju, I mean, the Pastor is dead?

175
00:12:07,125 --> 00:12:11,959
We don't know that.
We don't know who the Pastor is yet.

176
00:12:12,709 --> 00:12:14,459
At any rate,

177
00:12:14,459 --> 00:12:16,125
Eo Hyun Kyung

178
00:12:16,125 --> 00:12:17,918
is still alive.

179
00:12:17,918 --> 00:12:19,876
She's alive.

180
00:12:19,876 --> 00:12:21,250
She's alive.

181
00:12:21,250 --> 00:12:23,083
Let's not relax just yet.

182
00:12:23,626 --> 00:12:26,709
If Na Hae Ju is not the Pastor,

183
00:12:26,709 --> 00:12:30,375
it's likely that the Pastor
used Na Hae Ju to hide behind her.

184
00:12:30,375 --> 00:12:33,918
If Detective Eo found out who the Pastor is…

185
00:12:33,918 --> 00:12:36,375
given the Pastor's tendency
of leaving no loose end,

186
00:12:36,375 --> 00:12:38,542
there's no telling what will happen.

187
00:13:30,417 --> 00:13:32,459
This won't do.

188
00:13:32,459 --> 00:13:36,292
This the best footage I found,
but the image quality is so poor.

189
00:13:36,292 --> 00:13:39,500
I can't even identify models, not to mention number plates.

190
00:13:43,334 --> 00:13:45,209
[Incoming Call]

191
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,500
Hold on a minute.

192
00:13:56,417 --> 00:13:59,042
- Cha Yeon Ho speaking.
- Myeong Heon Jo here.

193
00:13:59,042 --> 00:14:03,125
You remember the anonymous caller
who reported the Pastor?

194
00:14:03,125 --> 00:14:04,792
- Are you listening?
- Yes, I am.

195
00:14:04,792 --> 00:14:06,834
Guess who it was.

196
00:14:06,834 --> 00:14:08,792
It was Na Hae Ju.

197
00:14:08,792 --> 00:14:12,667
We tracked the IP, which
led to an internet cafe.

198
00:14:12,667 --> 00:14:17,417
So we pulled the CCTV clips there,
and we spotted Na Hae Ju there.

199
00:14:17,417 --> 00:14:19,167
So, she was killed because…

200
00:14:19,167 --> 00:14:21,542
They found out she ratted them out,

201
00:14:21,542 --> 00:14:25,626
or there was infighting within the ring.

202
00:14:29,542 --> 00:14:32,667
But why are you telling me this?

203
00:14:32,667 --> 00:14:35,876
What do you mean? We work together.

204
00:14:35,876 --> 00:14:39,000
Let's share what we find from now on, okay?

205
00:14:43,417 --> 00:14:44,709
How adorable.

206
00:14:48,542 --> 00:14:50,375
Who was it?

207
00:14:50,375 --> 00:14:52,167
Captain Myeong.

208
00:14:53,876 --> 00:14:56,417
Na Hae Ju was the anonymous caller.

209
00:14:56,417 --> 00:14:58,542
She was the informant?

210
00:14:58,542 --> 00:15:02,125
Then she can't be the Pastor.

211
00:15:02,125 --> 00:15:03,167
That's right.

212
00:15:03,167 --> 00:15:05,125
Does it mean...

213
00:15:05,125 --> 00:15:07,709
Na Hae Ju was a victim,
like Kim Mi Yeong and Park Da Eun?

214
00:15:07,709 --> 00:15:09,792
It's too early to tell.

215
00:15:09,792 --> 00:15:12,083
She may be a victim-turned-offender.

216
00:15:12,083 --> 00:15:13,709
She may be dead,

217
00:15:13,709 --> 00:15:16,125
but it doesn't remove her from the suspect list.

218
00:15:17,834 --> 00:15:19,042
Wait.

219
00:15:20,042 --> 00:15:22,125
When did you get

220
00:15:22,125 --> 00:15:25,000
- so close with Captain Myeong?
- I did not.

221
00:15:25,584 --> 00:15:27,250
I wouldn't say 'close.'

222
00:15:28,042 --> 00:15:29,667
You're so suspicious.

223
00:15:32,250 --> 00:15:33,751
Superintendent.

224
00:15:34,834 --> 00:15:36,000
To the hospital!

225
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,000
What hospital?

226
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,667
She woke up!

227
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:41,209
- Park Da Eun!
- Park...

228
00:15:41,209 --> 00:15:42,334
I'll go now.

229
00:15:42,334 --> 00:15:44,334
- Thank you, ma'am!
- I'm heading out!

230
00:15:44,334 --> 00:15:46,375
[Park Da Eun]

231
00:15:53,167 --> 00:15:54,375
Excuse me.

232
00:15:54,375 --> 00:15:56,626
We're from the police.

233
00:15:56,626 --> 00:15:58,042
We have a few questions.

234
00:15:58,042 --> 00:16:00,500
- She's not fully-
- It's fine.

235
00:16:01,792 --> 00:16:03,459
Thank you.

236
00:16:12,751 --> 00:16:13,959
How's my baby doing?

237
00:16:13,959 --> 00:16:16,459
She's safe. Don't worry.

238
00:16:22,542 --> 00:16:24,042
How about Mi Yeong?

239
00:16:32,417 --> 00:16:33,918
So she is…

240
00:16:35,209 --> 00:16:36,751
And Hae Ju too…?

241
00:16:43,125 --> 00:16:46,792
What was your relationship with Na Hae Ju?

242
00:16:49,209 --> 00:16:50,834
She…

243
00:16:53,209 --> 00:16:55,918
dragged me into this hell.

244
00:16:57,250 --> 00:16:58,959
But she also…

245
00:16:59,792 --> 00:17:04,083
desperately tried to pull me out.

246
00:17:05,042 --> 00:17:08,334
Hae Ju hooked me up with the lender.

247
00:17:08,334 --> 00:17:10,626
I borrowed two million at first.

248
00:17:10,626 --> 00:17:12,876
A year later,

249
00:17:12,876 --> 00:17:14,792
it grew to 300 million.

250
00:17:14,792 --> 00:17:17,209
It was the same for Mi Yeong.

251
00:17:18,292 --> 00:17:20,918
Why didn't you call the police?

252
00:17:21,751 --> 00:17:23,834
The police…

253
00:17:23,834 --> 00:17:26,667
I did call them.

254
00:17:26,667 --> 00:17:28,459
But they said

255
00:17:28,459 --> 00:17:33,083
they couldn't investigate
based on statements alone.

256
00:17:33,083 --> 00:17:35,959
They told us to collect evidence first.

257
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,083
There was

258
00:17:39,083 --> 00:17:41,792
nothing we could do.

259
00:17:41,792 --> 00:17:44,542
When the police turned us down,

260
00:17:46,542 --> 00:17:49,000
we thought about ending it,

261
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,959
ending it all together.

262
00:18:04,083 --> 00:18:05,876
Here. Take it easy.

263
00:18:14,918 --> 00:18:16,834
Did you know...

264
00:18:16,834 --> 00:18:21,751
Na Hae Ju called the FSS about the Pastor's ring?

265
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:26,417
She did that for us.

266
00:18:27,918 --> 00:18:30,167
She did that to save us.

267
00:18:32,083 --> 00:18:35,250
Sign here, and we will proceed with the transfer.

268
00:18:35,250 --> 00:18:39,751
A single mom she recruited died in a car crash.

269
00:18:39,751 --> 00:18:42,167
She was not a drinker,
but she was drunk at the time.

270
00:18:42,167 --> 00:18:44,334
You must have meant a lot to her.

271
00:18:44,334 --> 00:18:46,042
Even more than family.

272
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:50,834
Sorry for your loss. I hope you find comfort.

273
00:18:59,167 --> 00:19:02,417
She couldn't do it anymore,

274
00:19:02,417 --> 00:19:04,209
getting single moms to

275
00:19:04,209 --> 00:19:06,918
sign up for death insurance.

276
00:19:07,834 --> 00:19:09,417
After that,

277
00:19:09,417 --> 00:19:11,751
Hae Ju paid us a visit.

278
00:19:12,417 --> 00:19:14,250
Told me to lay low for a while.

279
00:19:14,250 --> 00:19:16,667
She said she would report the Pastor.

280
00:19:17,876 --> 00:19:19,792
That it was the only way

281
00:19:20,834 --> 00:19:22,959
we could live.

282
00:19:24,292 --> 00:19:28,292
<i>I'm sure the baby's sleeping.
If you want to save it,</i>

283
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:30,167
<i>come out quietly alone.</i>

284
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:43,334
Get out!

285
00:20:47,125 --> 00:20:49,417
Do you remember the Pastor's face?

286
00:20:51,876 --> 00:20:54,292
No, because of the hat and the mask.

287
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:58,459
I don't even know if it was the Pastor.

288
00:21:27,459 --> 00:21:30,709
<i>Driving for the family.</i>

289
00:21:40,459 --> 00:21:41,959
Huh?

290
00:22:01,751 --> 00:22:03,250
What's this?

291
00:22:06,834 --> 00:22:08,751
Come on!

292
00:22:10,626 --> 00:22:12,417
[Same-Day Loan]

293
00:22:17,959 --> 00:22:19,667
We got a 112 call.

294
00:22:19,667 --> 00:22:22,626
The caller found bloody loan ad cards
dropped from a vehicle ahead.

295
00:22:22,626 --> 00:22:25,292
A black Forbidden, last digits 1139.

296
00:22:25,292 --> 00:22:29,125
It's moving west on Local Road 38.

297
00:22:39,167 --> 00:22:41,709
[Seoul Urban Integrated Information Center]
Contact the Command Center

298
00:22:41,709 --> 00:22:43,626
and open all CCTV channels in nearby areas.

299
00:22:43,626 --> 00:22:44,667
Yes, Ma'am.

300
00:22:44,667 --> 00:22:46,959
Dong Gi, request local police cooperation.

301
00:22:46,959 --> 00:22:48,209
Got it.

302
00:22:48,792 --> 00:22:51,209
Set up checkpoints at toll gates,
byways, and intersections

303
00:22:51,209 --> 00:22:52,751
connected to the westbound 38 road.

304
00:22:52,751 --> 00:22:56,125
Tell them to check all cars
of the same model as the suspect vehicle.

305
00:22:56,125 --> 00:22:57,500
Okay.

306
00:23:11,042 --> 00:23:13,125
Here! A black Forbidden.

307
00:23:16,709 --> 00:23:18,209
The vehicle exited to the right

308
00:23:18,209 --> 00:23:20,417
right before the checkpoint.

309
00:23:49,083 --> 00:23:51,459
The things you do to survive.

310
00:23:51,459 --> 00:23:54,000
You're now wanted across the country.

311
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,918
It's a matter of time before you get caught.

312
00:23:55,918 --> 00:23:58,876
It's not too late to turn yourself in,
before it gets uglier for you.

313
00:23:58,876 --> 00:24:00,292
Turn myself in?

314
00:24:02,876 --> 00:24:05,000
And you think I'll let you live?

315
00:24:13,209 --> 00:24:16,292
Look closely. They can be hiding anywhere.

316
00:24:16,292 --> 00:24:18,000
That one there.

317
00:24:28,334 --> 00:24:30,500
That's the car. I'm positive.

318
00:24:32,876 --> 00:24:34,292
Stop the car! Stop!

319
00:24:34,292 --> 00:24:36,042
Stop the car!

320
00:26:58,167 --> 00:26:59,792
Get out.

321
00:26:59,792 --> 00:27:01,584
Get out, you bastard!

322
00:27:02,334 --> 00:27:03,834
Come here.

323
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:08,542
How is Eo Hyun Kyung?

324
00:27:08,542 --> 00:27:10,042
Is she all right?

325
00:27:10,792 --> 00:27:12,334
She's not here.

326
00:27:13,375 --> 00:27:16,292
[Same Day Loan Call And Ask]

327
00:27:17,417 --> 00:27:19,209
Where's the kidnapped officer?

328
00:27:20,250 --> 00:27:23,167
Let me see your face, punk.

329
00:27:23,167 --> 00:27:25,125
Where is Hyun Kyung!

330
00:27:26,918 --> 00:27:28,626
Speak.

331
00:27:28,626 --> 00:27:29,792
Hey!

332
00:27:29,792 --> 00:27:32,500
Where is Eo Hyun Kyung!

333
00:27:34,042 --> 00:27:35,584
Is that…

334
00:27:35,584 --> 00:27:36,667
the Pastor?

335
00:27:36,667 --> 00:27:39,709
Not confirmed yet. He claims he is.

336
00:27:40,292 --> 00:27:43,500
We need to find Hyun Kyung first.

337
00:27:43,500 --> 00:27:46,000
Butter him up. We need him to talk.

338
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:47,250
Okay.

339
00:27:49,500 --> 00:27:51,000
Let me do it.

340
00:28:15,667 --> 00:28:17,292
Take off the cap.

341
00:28:19,792 --> 00:28:21,292
Do it.

342
00:28:25,167 --> 00:28:26,667
The mask, too.

343
00:28:34,834 --> 00:28:36,834
Where's Eo Hyun Kyung?

344
00:28:42,209 --> 00:28:45,417
You don't want the situation to get worse.

345
00:28:46,834 --> 00:28:49,667
- Where is she?
- Get me a lawyer.

346
00:28:49,667 --> 00:28:51,584
Not saying anything until you do.

347
00:29:05,042 --> 00:29:06,918
We got to make sure she's okay.

348
00:29:06,918 --> 00:29:10,500
If something happens to her,
it's all over for you, lawyer or not.

349
00:29:14,042 --> 00:29:17,626
So, like I said, get me a lawyer.

350
00:29:19,709 --> 00:29:21,876
Before it's all over.

351
00:29:47,292 --> 00:29:51,417
The nerve of that guy, demanding a lawyer.

352
00:29:51,417 --> 00:29:53,375
Something feels off.

353
00:29:53,375 --> 00:29:55,500
It's like he let himself get arrested.

354
00:29:56,167 --> 00:29:57,667
Because of the wanted notice?

355
00:29:57,667 --> 00:29:59,417
That's for the vehicle.

356
00:29:59,417 --> 00:30:01,459
We hadn't identified the Pastor.

357
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:05,209
If they just dumped the car and fled
with Detective Eo, no one would know.

358
00:30:05,209 --> 00:30:08,542
Why hide Detective Eo and get arrested?

359
00:30:08,542 --> 00:30:10,792
You're right. Why?

360
00:30:14,375 --> 00:30:15,751
What's this?

361
00:30:17,667 --> 00:30:19,918
Where are you taking him?

362
00:30:22,209 --> 00:30:24,918
NOI is taking him into custody.

363
00:30:24,918 --> 00:30:28,292
- Like hell you are. You know how we've-
- Lieutenant.

364
00:30:32,542 --> 00:30:34,375
Don't take it personally.

365
00:30:34,375 --> 00:30:37,209
I'll call you if something comes up.

366
00:30:44,834 --> 00:30:47,167
It's Lee Tae Ju all over again.

367
00:30:47,167 --> 00:30:50,083
That opportunistic son of a-

368
00:30:52,709 --> 00:30:53,667
Dong Gi, what's up?

369
00:30:53,667 --> 00:30:55,626
We got a call from NFS.

370
00:30:55,626 --> 00:30:59,042
They found something weird from Na Hae Ju's body.

371
00:31:01,125 --> 00:31:02,751
Something weird?

372
00:31:03,709 --> 00:31:05,626
It was in her stomach.

373
00:31:05,626 --> 00:31:08,667
We found an object while cleaning out its content.

374
00:31:08,667 --> 00:31:11,292
- Here.
- Does it mean she swallowed it?

375
00:31:11,292 --> 00:31:14,042
Yes. Most content was dissolved.

376
00:31:14,042 --> 00:31:16,417
This is plastic, so it remained intact.

377
00:31:16,417 --> 00:31:19,250
Is it likely that she was forced to swallow it?

378
00:31:19,250 --> 00:31:22,626
There was no damage on the oral mucosa.

379
00:31:22,626 --> 00:31:24,542
But we can't be sure it was voluntary.

380
00:31:24,542 --> 00:31:27,375
However, there was no sign of damage.

381
00:31:31,375 --> 00:31:34,209
It may not work. I mean, it was in her stomach.

382
00:31:34,209 --> 00:31:35,626
Hey, it works!

383
00:31:35,626 --> 00:31:37,000
There's an "Event" folder.

384
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:38,751
Looks like dash cam footage.

385
00:31:38,751 --> 00:31:40,375
Open the last one.

386
00:31:40,375 --> 00:31:41,667
Okay.

387
00:31:51,417 --> 00:31:55,834
It's from the car that Na Hae Ju rode.
The clip's taken right before the crash.

388
00:31:55,834 --> 00:31:58,876
Na Hae Ju swallowed it right before her death.

389
00:31:58,876 --> 00:32:00,459
She tried to show us something.

390
00:32:00,459 --> 00:32:03,209
- Dong Gi, rewind the clip.
- Okay.

391
00:32:10,125 --> 00:32:12,250
- This car!
- This is…

392
00:32:12,250 --> 00:32:14,334
The Black Forbidden 1139, right?

393
00:32:14,334 --> 00:32:16,042
The one that took Hyun Kyung.

394
00:32:16,042 --> 00:32:18,000
- Keep playing.
- Yes, sir.

395
00:32:23,834 --> 00:32:26,459
What's the deal with Mi Yeong and Da Eun?

396
00:32:27,042 --> 00:32:28,751
You didn't have to kill them.

397
00:32:28,751 --> 00:32:30,751
Shut your mouth, worm.

398
00:32:30,751 --> 00:32:32,918
You took everything they had.

399
00:32:32,918 --> 00:32:35,500
And now you want their death money?

400
00:32:35,500 --> 00:32:38,459
Son of a bitch, you're not even human.

401
00:32:39,125 --> 00:32:42,375
What the… this slut's tripping or what?

402
00:32:42,375 --> 00:32:44,000
Who do you think you owe your life to?

403
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:45,834
Have you forgotten everything?

404
00:32:45,834 --> 00:32:47,959
You were no better than those two.

405
00:32:47,959 --> 00:32:51,125
Without them, you'd have kicked the bucket.

406
00:32:51,125 --> 00:32:53,918
You want me to thrash you good?

407
00:32:53,918 --> 00:32:56,000
Wanna die like those two?

408
00:32:56,959 --> 00:32:59,792
Sure, but I won't die alone.

409
00:32:59,792 --> 00:33:02,083
Let me see your goddamn face first.

410
00:33:05,167 --> 00:33:08,167
Darn it!

411
00:33:10,792 --> 00:33:12,751
Don't!

412
00:34:13,709 --> 00:34:16,626
Go to hell!

413
00:34:46,667 --> 00:34:48,250
Goddamn it!

414
00:34:48,959 --> 00:34:51,375
Darn it!

415
00:35:19,083 --> 00:35:21,083
Good riddance, bitch.

416
00:36:22,334 --> 00:36:24,292
We arrested the fake one.

417
00:36:24,292 --> 00:36:26,584
They gave the real one time to run.

418
00:36:26,584 --> 00:36:27,876
So the one we arrested…

419
00:36:27,876 --> 00:36:29,959
Was one of the Pastor's lackeys.

420
00:36:29,959 --> 00:36:33,083
He has thoroughly hidden his identity.

421
00:36:33,083 --> 00:36:34,584
He must have thought out who

422
00:36:34,584 --> 00:36:37,042
would be arrested in his place.

423
00:36:37,042 --> 00:36:40,500
This is why Na Hae Ju swallowed the card.

424
00:36:43,417 --> 00:36:45,042
Wait, wait.

425
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:50,500
Isn't that him?

426
00:36:51,876 --> 00:36:53,334
That first guy in the tunnel.

427
00:36:53,334 --> 00:36:56,000
She just popped out in the tunnel.
How am I supposed to evade?

428
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:58,375
It's like she had a death wish.

429
00:36:58,375 --> 00:37:01,375
The driver who ran over Kim Mi Yeong.

430
00:37:01,375 --> 00:37:03,500
Samjeon Tunnel Crash records.

431
00:37:08,083 --> 00:37:09,667
Here.

432
00:37:16,417 --> 00:37:18,500
[Resident Registration Card Jang Gi Su]

433
00:37:20,417 --> 00:37:22,083
Exactly the same.

434
00:37:22,083 --> 00:37:23,500
So, this is the Pastor?

435
00:37:23,500 --> 00:37:26,083
He murdered Kim Mi Yeong and pretended

436
00:37:26,083 --> 00:37:27,667
to have ran her over by accident.

437
00:37:27,667 --> 00:37:29,834
That bastard!

438
00:37:30,667 --> 00:37:33,542
Let's run a background check first.

439
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:37,375
Hey! Anyone out there?

440
00:38:37,375 --> 00:38:39,292
Somebody? Anybody!

441
00:38:45,709 --> 00:38:48,167
You're not making any sense.

442
00:38:52,667 --> 00:38:57,584
You said that Ah Ju Im and Mag Sa Jang
kidnapped Detective Eo.

443
00:38:57,584 --> 00:38:59,584
And you don't know their faces?

444
00:39:01,667 --> 00:39:03,125
Look,

445
00:39:03,125 --> 00:39:06,584
what my client is saying is-

446
00:39:07,334 --> 00:39:08,834
Excuse me.

447
00:39:17,292 --> 00:39:20,334
I'm sorry, but I have to take this.

448
00:39:32,709 --> 00:39:34,876
I looked into Jang Gi Su's background.

449
00:39:35,584 --> 00:39:38,918
Three years ago,
he was arrested for insurance fraud.

450
00:39:38,918 --> 00:39:41,250
At the time, he had two accomplices.

451
00:39:41,250 --> 00:39:42,834
And?

452
00:39:43,667 --> 00:39:44,959
Look at their names.

453
00:39:44,959 --> 00:39:47,459
Gam Hee Seong, Im Ju Ah.

454
00:39:47,459 --> 00:39:48,459
[Gam Hee Seong. Im Ju Ah]

455
00:39:49,334 --> 00:39:51,125
[Jang Gi Su]

456
00:39:51,125 --> 00:39:52,667
If we flip Im Ju Ah…

457
00:39:52,667 --> 00:39:53,667
[Ah Ju Im]

458
00:39:53,667 --> 00:39:55,792
- Ah Ju Im?
- Ah Ju Im?

459
00:39:57,125 --> 00:39:58,709
- Ah Ju Im!
- Ah Ju Im!

460
00:39:58,709 --> 00:40:00,292
We saw that name at NOI.

461
00:40:00,292 --> 00:40:01,334
[Ah Ju Im: Insurance Fraud]

462
00:40:01,334 --> 00:40:03,125
[Mag Sa Jang: Used Car
Fraud Pastor: Ring Leader]

463
00:40:03,125 --> 00:40:05,542
The middle manager, working under the leader.

464
00:40:05,542 --> 00:40:09,042
Gam, when spelled backward, is Mag.

465
00:40:09,042 --> 00:40:10,542
Thus, Mag Sa Jang.

466
00:40:11,709 --> 00:40:13,792
Former partners in crime got back together

467
00:40:13,792 --> 00:40:16,334
to start an illegal loan business.

468
00:40:16,918 --> 00:40:19,334
They used nicknames

469
00:40:19,334 --> 00:40:21,459
to hide their identity.

470
00:40:27,209 --> 00:40:28,209
Has the package been sent?

471
00:40:28,209 --> 00:40:30,792
Yeah, must be in a container by now.

472
00:40:30,792 --> 00:40:31,959
Where to?

473
00:40:31,959 --> 00:40:34,334
How should I know?

474
00:40:35,959 --> 00:40:39,918
Well, there's this country
that ends in 'stan' or something.

475
00:40:39,918 --> 00:40:43,667
I paid the guys a few millions more,
and they promised no loose ends.

476
00:40:43,667 --> 00:40:45,167
Okay.

477
00:40:46,042 --> 00:40:48,667
Be careful when you recruit next time.

478
00:40:48,667 --> 00:40:52,500
That crazy bitch Na Hae Ju
almost ruined our operation.

479
00:40:53,626 --> 00:40:55,542
Good employees are hard to come by.

480
00:40:55,542 --> 00:40:59,375
That idiot bit the hand that fed her.

481
00:40:59,375 --> 00:41:01,792
Too lazy to work her way up the ladder.

482
00:41:05,542 --> 00:41:07,209
Keep an eye on the cop,

483
00:41:07,209 --> 00:41:09,584
until the ship leaves the port.

484
00:41:09,584 --> 00:41:12,792
- The guys there will do that.
- Hey.

485
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:17,292
Personally check on it.

486
00:41:19,500 --> 00:41:21,209
All right.

487
00:41:21,209 --> 00:41:23,709
No loose ends, huh? As always.

488
00:41:23,709 --> 00:41:25,876
It's so you.

489
00:41:25,876 --> 00:41:27,459
So uptight.

490
00:41:34,792 --> 00:41:36,918
Captain,

491
00:41:36,918 --> 00:41:38,959
I checked Gam Hee Seong's business records.

492
00:41:38,959 --> 00:41:42,250
He owns a car export business.

493
00:41:42,250 --> 00:41:46,167
Incheon Used Vehicle Export Complex,
Unit 12, Building 3.

494
00:41:46,167 --> 00:41:48,667
[Business Registration: Happy Used Car Export]
Used vehicle export.

495
00:41:50,584 --> 00:41:54,250
That reminds me. The car rental
where we found Hyun Kyung's blood,

496
00:41:54,250 --> 00:41:55,834
most vehicles there are illegal cars.

497
00:41:55,834 --> 00:41:58,250
Their vehicle identification numbers
have been erased.

498
00:41:58,250 --> 00:42:00,542
If they are exporting those cars-

499
00:42:00,542 --> 00:42:03,417
You mean they export illegal cars

500
00:42:03,417 --> 00:42:05,667
as part of a registered business.

501
00:42:06,292 --> 00:42:09,375
Where was the Pastor's car last spotted in CCTV?

502
00:42:09,375 --> 00:42:11,709
Local Road 38 Three-way Intersection Checkpoint.

503
00:42:11,709 --> 00:42:13,792
Dong Gi, put the map on the screen.

504
00:42:13,792 --> 00:42:16,083
- Dae Se, turn on the TV.
- Okay.

505
00:42:20,834 --> 00:42:22,375
[Incheon Export Complex]

506
00:42:22,375 --> 00:42:23,876
Okay.

507
00:42:27,876 --> 00:42:31,375
Here. It's close to the complex.

508
00:42:34,083 --> 00:42:35,334
Maybe the Pastor,

509
00:42:35,334 --> 00:42:37,542
his lackeys, and Hyun Kyung

510
00:42:37,542 --> 00:42:39,876
may all be in that location.

511
00:43:39,250 --> 00:43:40,751
Excuse me.

512
00:43:43,500 --> 00:43:47,542
If you poked your nose where it doesn't belong,
get the hell out of here.

513
00:43:47,542 --> 00:43:50,500
I speak Russian.

514
00:43:53,834 --> 00:43:55,042
How can I help you?

515
00:43:55,042 --> 00:43:57,292
I'm here to see the owner.

516
00:43:57,292 --> 00:43:59,042
Owner?

517
00:43:59,042 --> 00:44:00,834
What for?

518
00:44:00,834 --> 00:44:02,000
Police.

519
00:44:02,000 --> 00:44:05,209
- Gam Hee Seong. He's the owner, right?
- Oh.

520
00:44:06,083 --> 00:44:08,292
That was his name?

521
00:44:08,292 --> 00:44:11,083
He doesn't come here often, anyways.

522
00:44:11,083 --> 00:44:12,792
Call him if you need him.

523
00:44:12,792 --> 00:44:14,792
Where can I meet him?

524
00:44:16,209 --> 00:44:18,918
I wonder where.

525
00:44:18,918 --> 00:44:21,083
This talk kinda makes me want to see him.

526
00:44:21,083 --> 00:44:22,584
Get in line.

527
00:44:26,292 --> 00:44:27,834
What did he say?

528
00:44:27,834 --> 00:44:29,667
That he doesn't come here often.

529
00:44:29,667 --> 00:44:32,792
I don't think he is lying. Or is he? Damn it.

530
00:44:32,792 --> 00:44:34,417
Let's split up.

531
00:44:34,417 --> 00:44:36,334
Show them her picture, we might get something.

532
00:44:36,334 --> 00:44:37,292
- Okay.
- Will do.

533
00:44:37,292 --> 00:44:41,876
[Export / Scrap / Foreclosure
Call For Further Info]

534
00:44:41,876 --> 00:44:43,083
Have you seen this person?

535
00:44:43,083 --> 00:44:45,083
No idea. I didn't.

536
00:44:45,083 --> 00:44:48,042
- Are you sure?
- I really didn't.

537
00:44:48,042 --> 00:44:49,542
What about you?

538
00:44:49,542 --> 00:44:52,209
Beautiful.

539
00:44:52,209 --> 00:44:53,375
So pretty.

540
00:44:53,375 --> 00:44:55,042
Beautiful.

541
00:44:55,042 --> 00:44:57,292
You've got eyes at least.

542
00:44:57,292 --> 00:45:00,042
Investigator Cha, those guys are acting strange.

543
00:45:00,042 --> 00:45:02,876
